From 6ed3ad73047b7c9c21dc214aeed209ff04fd9b3c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Moskowski <me@corpix.ru>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 05:01:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] follow the kernel netlink changes for H1-H4 and keepalive

H1-H4 now travel as a packed u64 rather than a "start-end" string, and
persistent keepalive as a u32 carrying a packed u16 range. The CLI and
config file keep the human spelling: "N" for a single value, "lo-hi" for
a range, converted at the netlink boundary by awg_range_parse and
awg_range_format. A bad H range is now rejected before the set rather
than by the kernel.

PersistentKeepalive accepts the same two spellings; show prints "every
10 seconds to 30 seconds" for a range, and the dump column carries the
range verbatim.

AdvancedSecurity is gone, since the kernel no longer has a per-peer flag
and derives every feature from its configured values. That drops the
"advanced-security" set argument, the config key, and the showconf line.
parse_bool had no remaining callers.

netlink.h gains mnl_attr_put_u64 alongside the existing u16 and u32
helpers.
